    /* ---- submit button state machine ----
       Was: a bare textContent swap to "Submitting…" with no disabled styling, so
       the button stayed bright and clickable-looking through the whole request.
       Now the arrow leaves first (it's a promise of forward motion — it
       shouldn't sit there while we wait), a shimmer runs while in flight, and
       a "Submitted ✓" beat lands before the screen changes. */
    .brief .btn{ position:relative; overflow:hidden; }
